[{"text":"ApartFF[amp, {q1, q2, ...}] partial fractions loop integrals by decomposing them into simpler integrals that contain only linearly independent propagators. It uses FCApart as a backend and is equally suitable for 1-loop and multi-loop integrals.","anchor":"apartff"},{"text":"FCApart implements an algorithm based on arXiv:1204.2314 by F. Feng that seems to employ a variety Leinartas’s algorithm (cf. arXiv:1206.4740). Unlike Feng’s $Apart that is applicable to general multivariate polynomials, FCApart is tailored to work only with FeynCalc’s FeynAmpDenominator, Pair and CartesianPair symbols, i.e. it is less general in this respect.","anchor":"apartff"},{"text":"ApartFF[amp * extraPiece1, extraPiece2, {q1, q2, ...}] is a special working mode of ApartFF, where the final result of partial fractioning amp*extraPiece1 is multiplied by extraPiece2. It is understood, that extraPiece1*extraPiece2 should be unity, e. g. when extraPiece1 is an FAD, while extraPiece is an SPD inverse to it. This mode should be useful for nonstandard integrals where the desired partial fraction decomposition can be performed only after multiplying amp with extraPiece1.","anchor":"apartff"},{"text":"Overview, FCApart, FeynAmpDenominatorSimplify, FCLoopFindTensorBasis.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"FCClearScalarProducts[]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SPD[q, q] FAD[{q, m}] ApartFF[%, {q}]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{q^2}{q^2-m^2}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{m^2}{q^2-m^2}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SPD[q, p] SPD[q, r] FAD[{q}, {q - p}, {q - r}] ApartFF[%, {q}]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{(p\\cdot q) (q\\cdot r)}{q^2.(q-p)^2.(q-r)^2}\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{p^2 r^2}{4 q^2.(q-p)^2.(q-r)^2}+\\frac{p^2+2 (q\\cdot r)+2 r^2}{4 q^2.(-p+q+r)^2}+-\\frac{p^2}{4 q^2.(q-p)^2}-\\frac{r^2}{4 q^2.(q-r)^2}\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FAD[{q}, {q - p}, {q + p}] ApartFF[%, {q}]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{q^2.(q-p)^2.(p+q)^2}\\]","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{p^2 q^2.(q-p)^2}-\\frac{1}{p^2 q^2.(q-2 p)^2}\\]","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SPD[p, q1] SPD[p, q2]^2 FAD[{q1, m}, {q2, m}, q1 - p, q2 - p, q1 - q2] ApartFF[%, {q1, q2}]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{(p\\cdot \\;\\text{q1}) (p\\cdot \\;\\text{q2})^2}{\\left(\\text{q1}^2-m^2\\right).\\left(\\text{q2}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q1}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-p)^2.(\\text{q1}-\\text{q2})^2}\\]","anchor":"cb5-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SPD[q, p] FAD[{q, m}, {q - p, 0}] ApartFF[%, {q}]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{p\\cdot q}{\\left(q^2-m^2\\right).(q-p)^2}\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{m^2+p^2}{2 q^2.\\left((q-p)^2-m^2\\right)}-\\frac{1}{2 \\left(q^2-m^2\\right)}\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"If the propagators should not be altered via momentum shifts (e.g. because they belong to a previously identified topology), use the option FDS->False","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"int = SPD[q2, p] SPD[q1, p] FAD[{q1, m}, {q2, m}, q1 - p, q2 - p, q2 - q1]","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{(p\\cdot \\;\\text{q1}) (p\\cdot \\;\\text{q2})}{\\left(\\text{q1}^2-m^2\\right).\\left(\\text{q2}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q1}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-\\text{q1})^2}\\]","anchor":"cb7-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ApartFF[int, {q1, q2}]","anchor":"cb8","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{\\left(m^2+p^2\\right)^2}{4 \\left(\\text{q1}^2-m^2\\right).\\left(\\text{q2}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q1}-p)^2.(\\text{q1}-\\text{q2})^2.(\\text{q2}-p)^2}+\\frac{m^2+p^2}{2 \\;\\text{q1}^2.\\text{q2}^2.\\left((\\text{q1}-p)^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q1}-\\text{q2})^2}-\\frac{m^2+p^2}{2 \\left(\\text{q1}^2-m^2\\right).\\left(\\text{q2}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q1}-p)^2.(\\text{q1}-\\text{q2})^2}-\\frac{1}{2 \\left(\\text{q1}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q1}-\\text{q2})^2.(\\text{q2}-p)^2}+\\frac{1}{4 \\left(\\text{q1}^2-m^2\\right).\\left(\\text{q2}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q1}-\\text{q2})^2}\\]","anchor":"cb8-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ApartFF[int, {q1, q2}, FDS -> False]","anchor":"cb9","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{\\left(m^2+p^2\\right)^2}{4 \\left(\\text{q1}^2-m^2\\right).\\left(\\text{q2}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q1}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-\\text{q1})^2}+\\frac{m^2+p^2}{4 \\left(\\text{q1}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q1}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-\\text{q1})^2}-\\frac{m^2+p^2}{4 \\left(\\text{q1}^2-m^2\\right).\\left(\\text{q2}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q1}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-\\text{q1})^2}-\\frac{m^2+p^2}{4 \\left(\\text{q1}^2-m^2\\right).\\left(\\text{q2}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q2}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-\\text{q1})^2}+\\frac{m^2+p^2}{4 \\left(\\text{q2}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q1}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-\\text{q1})^2}-\\frac{1}{4 \\left(\\text{q1}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q2}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-\\text{q1})^2}-\\frac{1}{4 \\left(\\text{q2}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q1}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-\\text{q1})^2}+\\frac{1}{4 \\left(\\text{q1}^2-m^2\\right).\\left(\\text{q2}^2-m^2\\right).(\\text{q2}-\\text{q1})^2}+\\frac{1}{4 (\\text{q1}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-p)^2.(\\text{q2}-\\text{q1})^2}\\]","anchor":"cb9-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"If the partial fractioning should be performed only w. r. t. the denominators but not numerators, use the option Numerator->False","anchor":"cb9-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"int = FAD[k, p - k, {k, m}] SPD[p, k]","anchor":"cb10","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{k\\cdot p}{k^2.(p-k)^2.\\left(k^2-m^2\\right)}\\]","anchor":"cb10-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ApartFF[int, {k}]","anchor":"cb11","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{m^2+p^2}{2 m^2 k^2.\\left((k-p)^2-m^2\\right)}+-\\frac{1}{2 m^2 \\left(k^2-m^2\\right)}-\\frac{p^2}{2 m^2 k^2.(k-p)^2}\\]","anchor":"cb11-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ApartFF[int, {k}, Numerator -> False]","anchor":"cb12","section":"Examples"}]